reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-141-  // ---- exact mixed Int/Float comparison ------------------------------------
reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-142-  // The old rules compared via intToF(I), which ROUNDS ints >= 2^53 to a nearby
reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-143-  // double (so e.g. 9007199254740993 > 9007199254740992.0 came out false). Compare
reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-144-  // the REAL values instead: for a finite float F and an integer I,
reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-145-  //     F <  I   <=>   floor(F) <  I
reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-146-  //     F >  I   <=>   ceil(F)  >  I
reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-147-  //     F == I   <=>   F is integral  AND  floor(F) == I
reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-148-  // floorFloat/ceilFloat are exact and Float2Int yields the EXACT integer of an
reference-semantics/semantics/float.k:149:  // integral float (no rounding), so this is exact for every finite F. Non-finite
reference-semantics/semantics/float.k:150:  // F keeps the old intToF path (rounding is irrelevant to +/-inf and NaN, and
reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-151-  // inf/NaN have no integer floor). Opaque for kprove, [concrete] for krun.
reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-152-  syntax Bool ::= eqF(Float, Float) [function, total, symbol(eqF), no-evaluators]
reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-153-  rule eqF(F1:Float, F2:Float) => F1 ==Float F2 [concrete]
reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-154-
