reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-156-  rule floatFinite(F:Float) => notBool isNaN(F) andBool notBool isInfinite(F) [concrete]
reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-157-
reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-158-  syntax Bool ::= ltFI(Float, Int) [function, total, symbol(ltFI), no-evaluators]   // F <  I
reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-159-                | ltIF(Int, Float) [function, total, symbol(ltIF), no-evaluators]   // I <  F
reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-160-                | eqIF(Int, Float) [function, total, symbol(eqIF), no-evaluators]   // I == F
reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-161-  rule ltFI(F:Float, I:Int) => Float2Int(floorFloat(F)) <Int I  requires floatFinite(F)          [concrete]
reference-semantics/semantics/float.k-162-  rule ltFI(F:Float, I:Int) => floatLt(F, intToF(I))            requires notBool floatFinite(F)   [concrete]
